A. Commit message:
btrfs: avoid monopolizing a core when activating a swap file

B. Change summary:
During swap activation, we iterate over the extents of a file and can have many thousands of them, leading to a busy loop that monopolizes a core. This patch introduces a voluntary reschedule after processing each extent to prevent this issue.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/fs/btrfs/inode.c b/fs/btrfs/inode.c
index <old_version_hash>..<new_version_hash> 100644
--- a/fs/btrfs/inode.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/inode.c
@@ -10078,6 +10078,8 @@ static int btrfs_swap_activate(struct swap_info_struct *sis, struct file *file,
 			ret = -EINTR;
 			goto out;
 		}
+
+		cond_resched();
 	}
 
 	if (bsi.block_len)
```